                    insight_ambidextrous:   `Creative engine sustained: you ran the genuine pattern — slack channelled through healthy communities, a balanced explore/exploit split, an emergent stage-gate funnel, and the connectors retained. Idea throughput held, time-to-prototype stayed short, and the funded portfolio returned. The franchise paid the bills while the pipeline refilled behind it.`,
                    insight_cutslack:       `Quarter optimised, future empty: scrapping the slack secured this year’s ship date and dissolved the communities that generate hits. Throughput is collapsing on a lag and the pipeline is bare just as the franchise fades — you optimised the quarter and emptied the future. Slack was creative infrastructure, not idle waste.`,
                    insight_overswing:      `Over-swing to exploration: chasing the board’s IP demand, you funded too many bets and starved the franchise sequel that funds everything. Most exploration bets fail by nature, and the cash gap opened before any of them could ship. Ambidexterity is a managed balance, not a swing to the opposite extreme.`,
                    insight_managed:        `Communities managed to death: imposing quotas and deliverables turned communities of knowing into committees, and voluntary participation collapsed. Intrinsic motivation and trust — not assigned KPIs — are what make these communities generate ideas. You can enable a community or manage it, never both.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A mixed outcome: parts of the creative engine held, but slack governance, the explore/exploit balance and the pipeline discipline didn’t fully reinforce each other — enough leaks that the future pipeline is thinner than it looks and the cliff is still ahead.`,
                    insight_ungoverned:     `Slack without structure: you protected the hours and paid the full ~CA$9M production-capacity cost, but handed them out as unfocused free time instead of channelling them through the communities — so they never became shared experiments and throughput barely moved. Protecting slack and stewarding it through communities are different acts; only the second one feeds the pipeline.`,
                    insight_connectors:     `You lost the key connectors: declining the CA$400K counter let two knowledge brokers walk, and their departure fractured the communities far beyond their headcount. The rendering guild and gameplay community siloed into projects and time-to-prototype doubled — the disproportionate network value of brokers, learned the hard way.`,
                    insight_engagement_low: `Community engagement never recovered: without protected, stewarded slack the voluntary participation that fuels the funnel kept eroding, and idea throughput follows engagement down with a lag you’ll feel next year.`,
                    insight_ttp_high:       `Time-to-prototype ballooned: with the communities weakened and the connectors strained, concepts that once reached prototype in ~14 weeks now stall past 30 — meaning little will be ready when the franchise revenue fades.`,
                    insight_sequel:         `The franchise sequel slipped: either heavy ungoverned slack or an over-swing to exploration ate the production capacity the 9-month ship date needed. The proven title funds the gap before new IP arrives — slip it and the cash runway shortens dangerously.`,
                    insight_roi_negative:   `Innovation ROI came in negative: a disengaged, slow creative engine with no real stage-gate burned budget on bets that won’t return. ROI is a lagging confirmation of the leading indicators you let fall — engagement, slack, connectors and time-to-prototype.`,

                    hint_connectors:        `You’ve lost the key connectors — time-to-prototype is now capped high and the communities are fracturing. Restore engagement fast; some network value is irreplaceable once it walks.`,
                    hint_cutslack:          `Slack is at zero — the communities are withering and throughput will keep collapsing on a lag. Restore protected slack and channel it through the communities before the pipeline empties.`,
                    hint_engagement:        `Community engagement is dangerously low — the engine that generates ideas is stalling. Steward the communities and protect the slack that fuels them before throughput follows.`,
                    hint_managed:           `You’re managing the communities like project teams — quotas killed the voluntary participation that makes them work. Pull back the mandates and enable, don’t command.`,
                    hint_overswing:         `You’ve over-swung to exploration and the franchise sequel is slipping — the title that funds the gap. Rebalance toward a managed split before the cash runway shortens.`,
                    hint_ttp:               `Time-to-prototype is stretching toward stall — slack and the communities aren’t feeding the funnel fast enough. Retain the connectors and channel slack through the communities to bring it back down.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — engagement, throughput and time-to-prototype are all healthy. Land it: a real stage-gate and retaining the connectors will turn the engine into Innovation ROI.`,

